   "products": "<ul><li><strong>OpenCV calib3d module</strong> — calibrateCamera, findChessboardCorners, solvePnP, projectPoints, and undistortion <sup class=\"cite\">[1]</sup></li><li><strong>OpenCV ChArUco support</strong> — CharucoBoard, CharucoDetector, and matchImagePoints in the objdetect module of OpenCV 4.x <sup class=\"cite\">[3]</sup></li><li><strong>MATLAB Computer Vision Toolbox</strong> — single-camera calibration with reprojection error plots and parameter standard errors <sup class=\"cite\">[4]</sup></li></ul>",
   "misconception": {
    "myth": "<p>A low reprojection error proves the calibration is accurate.</p>",
    "reality": "<p>The error is measured on the same images used to fit the model, so it shows how well the model fits those views, not how well it predicts new ones. If every image shows the board flat-on at one distance, the data cannot separate the parameters well, which is why OpenCV asks for tilted views across the working range <sup class=\"cite\">[1]</sup> and Zhang's method needs differently oriented views <sup class=\"cite\">[2]</sup>. Check per-image errors and parameter uncertainties, which calibrateCameraExtended returns <sup class=\"cite\">[1]</sup>, and verify by measuring a known object at the working distance.</p>"
   },
   "keyNumbers": "<ul><li>Reprojection error: 0.19 px in MathWorks' example and 0.31 px in a fixed OpenCV forum case, versus 112 px when point order was wrong <sup class=\"cite\">[4]</sup><sup class=\"cite\">[5]</sup>; depends on corner detection, blur, and lens quality</li><li>Minimum views: 2 board orientations in theory <sup class=\"cite\">[2]</sup>; many more, with varied tilt and distance, in practice <sup class=\"cite\">[1]</sup></li><li>Distortion terms: 5 in the common model (k1, k2, p1, p2, k3), up to 14 in OpenCV's full model <sup class=\"cite\">[1]</sup></li><li>Millimeters per pixel ≈ working distance x pixel size / focal length; 600 mm x 3.45 µm / 12 mm ≈ 0.17 mm</li></ul>",
   "specs": null,
   "code": {
    "lang": "python",
    "text": "import cv2\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Describe the physical board: 7 x 5 squares, 30 mm squares, 22 mm markers.\n# Measure the printed board with calipers and use the measured sizes.\ndictionary = cv2.aruco.getPredefinedDictionary(cv2.aruco.DICT_5X5_100)\nboard = cv2.aruco.CharucoBoard((7, 5), 30.0, 22.0, dictionary)   # units: mm\ndetector = cv2.aruco.CharucoDetector(board)\n\nobj_points, img_points = [], []\nfor path in calibration_image_paths:          # 20-30 photos: tilted, near and far, reaching the corners\n    gray = cv2.imread(path, cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE)\n    ch_corners, ch_ids, _, _ = detector.detectBoard(gray)\n    if ch_ids is None or len(ch_ids) < 6:     # too few corners found: skip this view\n        continue\n    obj, img = board.matchImagePoints(ch_corners, ch_ids)   # 3D board points <-> 2D pixels\n    obj_points.append(obj)\n    img_points.append(img)\n\nimage_size = gray.shape[::-1]                 # (width, height)\nrms, K, dist, rvecs, tvecs = cv2.calibrateCamera(\n    obj_points, img_points, image_size, None, None)\n# K    = 3x3 camera matrix: fx, fy (focal length in pixels) and cx, cy (principal point)\n# dist = k1, k2, p1, p2, k3 (radial and tangential lens distortion)\nprint(\"overall RMS reprojection error (px):\", rms)\n\n# Per-view check: reproject the board with the fitted model and find views that disagree.\nfor i, (obj, img) in enumerate(zip(obj_points, img_points)):\n    projected, _ = cv2.projectPoints(obj, rvecs[i], tvecs[i], K, dist)\n    err = np.sqrt(np.mean(np.sum((projected - img) ** 2, axis=-1)))\n    if err > 2 * rms:\n        print(\"view\", i, \"error\", err, \"px: blurred, moved, or misdetected; drop it and rerun\")",
    "html": "<pre class=\"code\"><code data-lang=\"python\">import cv2\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Describe the physical board: 7 x 5 squares, 30 mm squares, 22 mm markers.\n# Measure the printed board with calipers and use the measured sizes.\ndictionary = cv2.aruco.getPredefinedDictionary(cv2.aruco.DICT_5X5_100)\nboard = cv2.aruco.CharucoBoard((7, 5), 30.0, 22.0, dictionary)   # units: mm\ndetector = cv2.aruco.CharucoDetector(board)\n\nobj_points, img_points = [], []\nfor path in calibration_image_paths:          # 20-30 photos: tilted, near and far, reaching the corners\n    gray = cv2.imread(path, cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE)\n    ch_corners, ch_ids, _, _ = detector.detectBoard(gray)\n    if ch_ids is None or len(ch_ids) &lt; 6:     # too few corners found: skip this view\n        continue\n    obj, img = board.matchImagePoints(ch_corners, ch_ids)   # 3D board points &lt;-&gt; 2D pixels\n    obj_points.append(obj)\n    img_points.append(img)\n\nimage_size = gray.shape[::-1]                 # (width, height)\nrms, K, dist, rvecs, tvecs = cv2.calibrateCamera(\n    obj_points, img_points, image_size, None, None)\n# K    = 3x3 camera matrix: fx, fy (focal length in pixels) and cx, cy (principal point)\n# dist = k1, k2, p1, p2, k3 (radial and tangential lens distortion)\nprint(&quot;overall RMS reprojection error (px):&quot;, rms)\n\n# Per-view check: reproject the board with the fitted model and find views that disagree.\nfor i, (obj, img) in enumerate(zip(obj_points, img_points)):\n    projected, _ = cv2.projectPoints(obj, rvecs[i], tvecs[i], K, dist)\n    err = np.sqrt(np.mean(np.sum((projected - img) ** 2, axis=-1)))\n    if err &gt; 2 * rms:\n        print(&quot;view&quot;, i, &quot;error&quot;, err, &quot;px: blurred, moved, or misdetected; drop it and rerun&quot;)</code></pre>"
   },
