    "companies": "<ul><li><strong>Nabtesco</strong> (Japan) — RV precision reducers; claims about 60% of the medium-to-large robot reducer market <sup class=\"cite\">[1]</sup>.</li><li><strong>Harmonic Drive Systems</strong> (Japan) — strain wave gears, gear heads, and actuators; Harmonic Drive LLC serves North America <sup class=\"cite\">[2]</sup><sup class=\"cite\">[7]</sup>.</li><li><strong>ATI Industrial Automation</strong> (US) — tool changers and force-torque sensors; listed as a brand of Novanta on Novanta's site <sup class=\"cite\">[3]</sup><sup class=\"cite\">[8]</sup>.</li><li><strong>Robotiq</strong> — cobot grippers, sensors, cameras, and workcells <sup class=\"cite\">[4]</sup>.</li><li><strong>Schmalz</strong> (Germany) — vacuum gripping; bought Soft Robotics' gripper business, including mGrip, in August 2024; Soft Robotics is now Oxipital AI <sup class=\"cite\">[5]</sup>.</li><li><strong>NVIDIA</strong> (US) — Jetson Thor onboard compute for robots <sup class=\"cite\">[6]</sup>.</li></ul>"
