   "speed": "Travel speed 75-225 m/min per axis (1.25-3.75 m/s), acceleration 2-10 m/s² <sup class=\"cite\">[1]</sup>",
   "notes": "<p>Spans whole machine bays and logistics areas, loading machine tools, palletizing, and packing; Güdel lists machine loading, palletizing, packaging, assembly, and battery handling among its FP gantry's uses <sup class=\"cite\">[1]</sup>. Each motor drives one straight axis directly, so there is no hard joint-angle math; it carries heavy loads (quoted in newtons and traded against speed) and repeats within ±0.02-0.1 mm, but its frame fills the space above the work and its tool can only come down from above <sup class=\"cite\">[1, 2]</sup>. On the cheese plate line it is the design choice for the outfeed if plates go into open-top racks or cases; sliding plates sideways onto shelves inside a closed trolley would need an arm instead. Reach here is the x-axis stroke of Güdel's FP series, roughly 5-10 m (its y strokes go up to 14 m on one heavy variant and its z strokes are 2-3 m) <sup class=\"cite\">[1]</sup>; the 2,000 mm drawing height is illustrative, not from a datasheet, and is low for an FP gantry, whose vertical axis alone travels 2-3 m.</p>",
